---
import WikiLayout from '../layouts/WikiLayout.astro';
import { base } from '../lib/base';
---

<WikiLayout title="Whats New?" description="Complete reference for all modded classes, rebalances, status effects, and systems in Idle Guild Master Modded v1.3.20.10.">
  <div class="docsContainer">
    <!-- Main Documentation Content -->
    <article class="docsMain">
      <!-- Page Header -->
      <header class="pageHeader">
        <div class="headerTop">
          <h1>What's New in IGM+</h1>
          <span class="versionBadge">v1.3.20.10 Active</span>
        </div>
        <p class="headerSubtitle">
          Comprehensive reference guide to all modded class trees, major class path rebalances, combat mechanics, status effects, equipment, and quality-of-life additions in Idle Guild Master Modded.
        </p>
      </header>

      <!-- Quick Navigation Bar for Small Screens -->
      <nav class="mobileQuickNav" aria-label="Quick Section Navigation">
        <span class="quickNavLabel">Jump to:</span>
        <div class="quickNavPills">
          <a href="#new-class-trees">New Classes</a>
          <a href="#class-rebalances">Class Rebalances</a>
          <a href="#summons-minions">Minions & Summons</a>
          <a href="#status-effects-combat">Status & Combat</a>
          <a href="#equipment-crafting">Equipment</a>
          <a href="#game-modes">Game Modes</a>
          <a href="#qol">Quality of Life</a>
        </div>
      </nav>

      <!-- SECTION 1: NEW CLASS TREES -->
      <section id="new-class-trees" class="docsSection">
        <div class="sectionHeader">
          <span class="sectionBadge">Classes</span>
          <h2>New Class Trees & Evolution Paths</h2>
          <p class="sectionDesc">IGM+ introduces an entirely new 5th base archetype—the Outlander—and a dedicated single-target burst mage branch for the Adept.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- 1.1 Outlander Tree -->
        <div id="outlander-tree" class="subSection">
          <div class="subHeader">
            <img src={`${base}/images/unit_outlander.png`} alt="Outlander" class="subIcon sprite" width="36" height="36" />
            <div>
              <h3>Outlander Class Tree (Tier 1–Tier 9)</h3>
              <p class="subTagline">Warrior Archetype · Axes & Light Armor · Multi-Strike Cleaves</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p>
            The <strong>Outlander</strong> is the 5th base class choice alongside Footman, Archer, Apprentice, and Rogue. Starting with innate multi-strike axe mastery via <strong>Wild Strikes I</strong>, the Outlander expands into 4 distinct promotion paths spanning from starter recruit all the way to Tier 9 pinnacle masteries:
          </p>

          <div class="classBranchGrid">
            <!-- Branch 1: Avatar of Wrath -->
            <div class="branchCard">
              <div class="branchCardHeader">
                <img src={`${base}/images/unit_avatar_of_wrath.png`} alt="Avatar of Wrath" class="sprite" width="28" height="28" />
                <div>
                  <h4>Avatar of Wrath Branch (T2–T9)</h4>
                  <span class="branchLine">Marauder &rarr; Barbarian &rarr; Berserker &rarr; Savage Berserker &rarr; Crimson Warlord &rarr; Blood Reaver &rarr; Scarlet Berserker &rarr; Avatar of Wrath</span>
                </div>
              </div>
              <p>
                Hyper-aggressive physical melee brawlers. Specializes in multi-strike flurry strikes, on-kill recasts (<em>Savage Cleave</em> recasts immediately on kill), and <strong>Savage Rage</strong> frenzy (+30% damage dealt, +30% damage taken) to tear down enemy frontlines in rapid succession.
              </p>
            </div>

            <!-- Branch 2: Beast Tamer -->
            <div class="branchCard">
              <div class="branchCardHeader">
                <img src={`${base}/images/unit_beast_tamer.png`} alt="Beast Tamer" class="sprite" width="28" height="28" />
                <div>
                  <h4>Beast Tamer Branch (T2–T9)</h4>
                  <span class="branchLine">Heathen &rarr; Brigand &rarr; Renegade &rarr; Rat Tamer &rarr; Cat Tamer &rarr; Bear Tamer &rarr; Beast Tamer</span>
                </div>
              </div>
              <p>
                Commands a loyal pack of <strong>7 Tamed Beast companions</strong>. When casting <em>Wild Strikes II</em>, the Tamer heals all active companion beasts for <strong>50%–150% of damage dealt</strong>, turning beast squads into resilient frontline sustain tanks that never suffer minion decay.
              </p>
            </div>

            <!-- Branch 3: Datura Hierophant -->
            <div class="branchCard">
              <div class="branchCardHeader">
                <img src={`${base}/images/unit_datura_hierophant.png`} alt="Datura Hierophant" class="sprite" width="28" height="28" />
                <div>
                  <h4>Datura Hierophant Branch (T3–T9)</h4>
                  <span class="branchLine">Druid &rarr; Forest Druid &rarr; Gloom Druid &rarr; Hemodruid &rarr; Bloodthorn Druid &rarr; Sanguine Druid &rarr; Datura Hierophant</span>
                </div>
              </div>
              <p>
                Nature magic controller and frontline ward. Restricts enemy mobility with <strong>Entangle</strong> (forces enemy dodge to 0% and reduces damage dealt by -20%) while wreathing party members in <strong>Thorns</strong> to reflect melee strike damage back at attackers.
              </p>
            </div>

            <!-- Branch 4: El Salvador -->
            <div class="branchCard">
              <div class="branchCardHeader">
                <img src={`${base}/images/unit_el_salvador_1.png`} alt="El Salvador" class="sprite" width="28" height="28" />
                <div>
                  <h4>El Salvador Branch (T3–T9)</h4>
                  <span class="branchLine">Exile &rarr; Desperado &rarr; El Salvador I &rarr; El Salvador II &rarr; El Salvador III &rarr; El Salvador</span>
                </div>
              </div>
              <p>
                High-agility duelist and counter-striker. Uses <strong>Evasion</strong> (+25% flat dodge chance), triggers immediate counterattacks upon evading enemy swings, and executes severely wounded enemies with <em>Rapid Exploitation</em>.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- 1.2 Arcanist Tree -->
        <div id="arcanist-tree" class="subSection">
          <div class="subHeader">
            <img src={`${base}/images/unit_singularity_magus.png`} alt="Singularity Magus" class="subIcon sprite" width="36" height="36" />
            <div>
              <h3>Singularity Magus Single-Target Burst Mage (Tier 3–Tier 9)</h3>
              <p class="subTagline">Adept 3rd Promotion Branch · Boss Executioner · Pure Aether Scaling</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p>
            A brand-new promotion option for the <strong>Adept</strong> alongside the Fire Wizard and Dark Sorcerer. Designed from the ground up as the premier single-target boss sniper in the Mage tree:
          </p>
          <div class="tierProgressionBox">
            <span class="progressionLabel">Promotion Path:</span>
            <div class="progressionSteps">
              <span class="stepBadge">T3 Arcanist</span> &rarr;
              <span class="stepBadge">T4 Spellweaver</span> &rarr;
              <span class="stepBadge">T5 Aether Mage</span> &rarr;
              <span class="stepBadge">T6 Aether Archmage</span> &rarr;
              <span class="stepBadge">T7 Disintegrator</span> &rarr;
              <span class="stepBadge">T8 Grand Magus</span> &rarr;
              <span class="stepBadge">T9 Singularity Magus</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="featureDetailsGrid">
            <div class="featureDetail">
              <h4>Disintegrate Spells</h4>
              <p>Active spells channel focused beams of concentrated aether, scaling up to <strong>3000% magic damage</strong> with a built-in <strong>20%–30% instant recast chance</strong> on cast.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="featureDetail">
              <h4>Aether Resonance</h4>
              <p>Passives bypass enemy taunt mechanics to lock directly onto Dungeon and Raid Bosses, piercing up to <strong>70% enemy magic defense</strong> and gaining massive Skill Amp.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- SECTION 2: CLASS PATH REBALANCES -->
      <section id="class-rebalances" class="docsSection">
        <div class="sectionHeader">
          <span class="sectionBadge">Rebalances</span>
          <h2>Class Path Rebalances (9 Branches)</h2>
          <p class="sectionDesc">
            Vanilla IGM suffered from several classes having flat static numbers that fell off into irrelevance in endgame, suicidal gimmicks, or dead passives. These 9 evolution branches have been extensively overhauled with modern scaling and impactful tactical kits.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Rebalance 1: Black Idol -->
        <div id="rebalance-black-idol" class="rebalanceCard">
          <div class="rebalanceHeader">
            <img src={`${base}/images/unit_black_idol.png`} alt="Black Idol" class="sprite" width="36" height="36" />
            <div>
              <h3>1. Black Idol Branch (Necromancer & Lich Line)</h3>
              <span class="rebalanceArchetype">Skill-Based Summoning · Soul Tether · Soul Harvest Cursed Death Scaling</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="rebalanceBody">
            <p><strong>The Vanilla Problem:</strong> Minions only spawned when an enemy died (making them useless against lone bosses), hard-capped at 1 minion total, 0 physical defense left Liches exposed to one-shots, and minions decayed at a punishing 25% HP per turn.</p>
            <p><strong>The Overhaul:</strong></p>
            <ul class="docsList">
              <li><strong>Skill-Based Summoning:</strong> Active Curse skills now directly summon undead servants mid-combat—no enemy death required.</li>
              <li><strong>Summon Capacity by Tier:</strong> Max summons scale up across tiers: <strong>1 minion at T4–T5</strong>, <strong>2 minions at T6–T7</strong>, and <strong>3 minions at T8–T9</strong>.</li>
              <li><strong>Capacity Mending:</strong> If active minions are already at max capacity, subsequent skill casts heal all active minions for <strong>35% of their Max HP</strong>.</li>
              <li><strong>Soul Tether (Damage Redirection):</strong> To safeguard the Lich's 0 DEF glass-cannon design, passives redirect <strong>20% (T4) up to 45% (T9)</strong> of all damage taken by the Lich distributed across their active living minions.</li>
              <li><strong>Soul Harvest Status Effect:</strong> Whenever a cursed enemy dies, all active minions absorb their soul, gaining permanent battle-long stacks: <strong>+15% Max HP</strong>, <strong>+10% Damage Dealt</strong>, and <strong>-5% Damage Taken</strong> per stack (up to 10 stacks at T9 = +150% HP, +100% DMG, -50% DMG taken!).</li>
              <li><strong>Reduced Minion Decay:</strong> Undead minion decay rates reduced from vanilla 25% down to tier-scaled rates: Zombie (20%), Skeleton (18%), Bone Horror (16%), Bone Nightmare (14%), Bone Abomination (12%), Bone Hydra (10%).</li>
              <li><strong>Summon Pool per Tier:</strong> T4 Necromancer &rarr; Zombie, T5 Demilich &rarr; Skeleton, T6 Lich &rarr; Bone Horror, T7 Ancient Lich &rarr; Bone Nightmare, T8 Lord of Decay &rarr; <strong>Bone Abomination (New Mod Minion)</strong>, T9 Black Idol &rarr; Bone Hydra.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Rebalance 2: Corrosive Wraith -->
        <div id="rebalance-corrosive-wraith" class="rebalanceCard">
          <div class="rebalanceHeader">
            <img src={`${base}/images/unit_corrosive_wraith.png`} alt="Corrosive Wraith" class="sprite" width="36" height="36" />
            <div>
              <h3>2. Corrosive Wraith Branch (Venomous Archer Line)</h3>
              <span class="rebalanceArchetype">Hybrid Weapon Scaling · Universal Damage Vulnerability · Stat Drain</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="rebalanceBody">
            <p><strong>The Vanilla Problem:</strong> Static flat poison damage fell off severely against high-health bosses, and 0-defense bosses made physical armor shred completely useless ($0 \times 4\% = 0$).</p>
            <p><strong>The Overhaul:</strong></p>
            <ul class="docsList">
              <li><strong>Progressive Hybrid Weapon Scaling (T6–T9):</strong> Bow attacks scale with both Dexterity and Intelligence starting at Tier 6: <strong>100% DEX + 30% INT (T6)</strong> &rarr; <strong>40% INT (T7)</strong> &rarr; <strong>50% INT (T8)</strong> &rarr; <strong>60% INT (T9)</strong>.</li>
              <li><strong>Corrosion (<span class="codeBadge">CORROSION</span>):</strong> Stackable universal damage vulnerability debuff lasting 3 turns. Target takes <strong>+4% damage taken from all sources per stack</strong> (capped at +12% at 3 stacks for T8 Wraith, and +20% at 5 stacks for T9 Corrosive Wraith). Multiplies both physical and magical damage for the entire party!</li>
              <li><strong>Enfeeble (<span class="codeBadge">ENFEEBLE</span>):</strong> Stackable stat reduction lasting 2 turns. Lowers the target's <strong>CON, DEX, and INT by -5% per stack</strong> (capped at -5% at 1 stack for T8 Wraith, and -15% at 3 stacks for T9 Corrosive Wraith), crippling boss offensive scaling.</li>
              <li><strong>Focused Barrage Active Skill:</strong> Fires 2 arrows per enemy (50% damage each), giving dual independent proc rolls per target for Corrosion and Enfeeble.</li>
              <li><strong>+15% Hit Chance Bonus:</strong> Granted a flat <span class="codeBadge">hitChanceBonus = 0.15</span> (+15% Hit Chance) across the branch (T4 Poison Bow &rarr; T9 Corrosive Wraith), maintaining steady status infliction while allowing evasion counterplay.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Rebalance 3: Eldritch Alchemist -->
        <div id="rebalance-eldritch-alchemist" class="rebalanceCard">
          <div class="rebalanceHeader">
            <img src={`${base}/images/unit_eldritch_alchemist.png`} alt="Eldritch Alchemist" class="sprite" width="36" height="36" />
            <div>
              <h3>3. Eldritch Alchemist Branch (Chemical Reaction Catalyst)</h3>
              <span class="rebalanceArchetype">Tiered Chemical Reactions · Vaporize & Thermal Shock · Catalytic Barrage</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="rebalanceBody">
            <p><strong>The Vanilla Problem:</strong> Alchemists were treated as "suicide bombers" that were useless dead weight while alive (weak unscaled physical attacks); players only wanted them to die immediately to trigger Thaumaturgy.</p>
            <p><strong>The Overhaul:</strong></p>
            <ul class="docsList">
              <li><strong>Tiered Chemical Reactions (Thaumaturgy I–IV):</strong> Basic attacks and skill arrows dynamically react with existing elemental debuffs on hit:
                <ul>
                  <li><strong>Vaporize (hitting Ablaze):</strong> Triggers AoE magic explosion dealing 0.6x INT (T6) up to 1.2x INT (T9) magic damage to all enemies.</li>
                  <li><strong>Thermal Shock (hitting Frozen, T7–T9):</strong> Shatters the freeze for massive bonus hybrid damage: <strong>+100% Phys / +100% Mag (T7)</strong> up to <strong>+150% Phys / +150% Mag (T9)</strong>.</li>
                  <li><strong>Brittle Toxin (T9 Capstone):</strong> Inflicts a flat <strong>+20% Damage Taken</strong> vulnerability for 2 turns (strictly non-stacking).</li>
                </ul>
              </li>
              <li><strong>Progressive Hybrid Weapon Scaling:</strong> 100% DEX + 30% INT (T6) &rarr; 40% (T7) &rarr; 50% (T8) &rarr; 60% (T9) with +15% Hit Chance bonus (<span class="codeBadge">hitChanceBonus = 0.15</span>).</li>
              <li><strong>Catalytic Barrage (T9 Active):</strong> Fires 3 random arrows triggering passive reactions, then detonates a full-field <em>Grand Chemical Detonation</em> applying Vaporize, Brittle Toxin, and Thermal Shock to ALL living enemies.</li>
              <li><strong>Supercharged Death Progression:</strong> Iconic on-death explosions preserved; reanimation via <em>Feeble Tether</em> grants <strong>10.0x Damage Amplification</strong> across Catalytic Barrage!</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Rebalance 4: Wyrm Rider -->
        <div id="rebalance-wyrm-rider" class="rebalanceCard">
          <div class="rebalanceHeader">
            <img src={`${base}/images/unit_wyrm_rider.png`} alt="Wyrm Rider" class="sprite" width="36" height="36" />
            <div>
              <h3>4. Wyrm Rider Branch (Mounted Beastmaster & Dragon Rider)</h3>
              <span class="rebalanceArchetype">Rider-Scaled Mount Attacks · Pure Mount Active Skills · Dual Elemental Breath</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="rebalanceBody">
            <p><strong>The Vanilla Problem:</strong> Mounts dealt a static 100 flat damage in endgame where bosses had 10,000+ HP; active skills were generic archer arrow volleys with zero draconic flavor.</p>
            <p><strong>The Overhaul:</strong></p>
            <ul class="docsList">
              <li><strong>Rider Stat-Scaled End-of-Turn Mount Attacks:</strong> Mount follow-up strikes scale directly from the Rider's <strong>DEX + INT</strong> (from 60% DEX at T4 up to <strong>120% DEX + 120% INT at T9</strong>), attack the enemy the Rider targeted, can roll Crits, and inflict <strong>Bleed</strong> (Poison for Spitfang).</li>
              <li><strong>Attack Range Split:</strong> Melee for T4–T5 mounts (Wolf Bite, Worg Maul), Ranged for T6–T9 mounts (Spitfang Spit, Drake Rake, Golden Rake, Wyrm Tear).</li>
              <li><strong>Pure Mount Active Skills:</strong> Archer arrow volleys replaced entirely with ferocious Mount abilities:
                <ul>
                  <li><strong>T4 Wolf Rider:</strong> <em>Savage Pounce</em> (250% Phys + 1-turn Stun).</li>
                  <li><strong>T5 Worg Rider:</strong> <em>Frenzied Rend</em> (3x 200% Phys + Bleed 20 stacks).</li>
                  <li><strong>T6 Spitfang Rider:</strong> <em>Caustic Deluge</em> (3x 220% Magic + Poison 3 turns).</li>
                  <li><strong>T7 Drake Rider:</strong> <em>Incinerate</em> (220% Magic AoE + Ablaze).</li>
                  <li><strong>T8 Golden Rider:</strong> <em>Incinerate II</em> (300% Magic AoE + Ablaze).</li>
                  <li><strong>T9 Wyrm Rider:</strong> <em>Sublimate</em> (cataclysmic twin breath: 200% Magic AoE + Ablaze, followed immediately by 200% Magic AoE + Frozen).</li>
                </ul>
              </li>
              <li><strong>Living Companion Synergy:</strong> Mount abilities scale with <span class="codeBadge">fromLivingCompanion</span> pet accessories and whips.</li>
              <li><strong>+15% Hit Chance Bonus:</strong> All mounts and riders in the branch (T3–T9) receive a flat <span class="codeBadge">hitChanceBonus = 0.15</span> (+15% Hit Chance) across their passives (Rider I–VII).</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Rebalance 5: Angel of War -->
        <div id="rebalance-angel-of-war" class="rebalanceCard">
          <div class="rebalanceHeader">
            <img src={`${base}/images/unit_angel_of_war.png`} alt="Angel of War" class="sprite" width="36" height="36" />
            <div>
              <h3>5. Angel of War Branch (Paladin & Frontline Auramancer)</h3>
              <span class="rebalanceArchetype">Radiant Blessing 4-in-1 Aura · Holy Cleansing & Shields · Anti-Undead Smite</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="rebalanceBody">
            <p><strong>The Vanilla Problem:</strong> Redundant darkness/silence meatshield with generic damage buffs that failed to provide the iconic holy protector fantasy.</p>
            <p><strong>The Overhaul:</strong></p>
            <ul class="docsList">
              <li><strong>Paladin / Auramancer Scaling:</strong> Threat 2 frontline protector scaling with <strong>100% CON + 70% INT</strong> across the branch. Basic attacks deal Physical damage; active skills deal Magic damage with <strong>+50% bonus damage vs Undead</strong> (T6–T9).</li>
              <li><strong>Radiant Blessing (4-in-1 Dynamic Battle Aura):</strong> Automatically wreathes all party members at battle start:
                <ul>
                  <li><strong>Status Immunity:</strong> +10% (T4) up to <strong>+50% (T9)</strong>.</li>
                  <li><strong>Damage vs Undead:</strong> +5% (T4) up to <strong>+30% (T9)</strong>.</li>
                  <li><strong>Flat Damage Reduction:</strong> +5 DR (T6) up to <strong>+15 DR (T9)</strong>.</li>
                  <li><strong>HP Regeneration:</strong> +3% Max HP/turn (T8) up to <strong>+5% Max HP/turn (T9)</strong>.</li>
                </ul>
              </li>
              <li><strong>Holy Sustain & Shields:</strong> Generic damage buffs removed. Skills cleanse party debuffs and grant holy shields scaling up to <strong>25% of each ally's Max HP</strong> on <em>Wrath of Heaven II</em>. Turn-start automatic cleanse on T8 and T9.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Rebalance 6: Black Regent -->
        <div id="rebalance-black-regent" class="rebalanceCard">
          <div class="rebalanceHeader">
            <img src={`${base}/images/unit_black_regent.png`} alt="Black Regent" class="sprite" width="36" height="36" />
            <div>
              <h3>6. Black Regent Branch (Dark Knight & Executioner)</h3>
              <span class="rebalanceArchetype">150% CON Weapon Scaling · Bloodflame Burn & Healing Block · Decimate Execute</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="rebalanceBody">
            <p><strong>The Overhaul:</strong></p>
            <ul class="docsList">
              <li><strong>Branch-Wide 150% CON Weapon Scaling:</strong> Extended 1.5x CON scaling across the entire Knight/Dark Knight branch: Knight, Dark Knight, Death Knight, Scourge, Tyrant, Overlord, and Black Regent. High-CON health pools now directly fuel devastating sword strikes.</li>
              <li><strong>Bloodflame (<span class="codeBadge">BLOODFLAME</span>):</strong> Curses targets to burn for <strong>5% of max Health each turn as magic damage</strong> and <strong>completely halts all healing</strong> (direct heals, lifesteal, regen).</li>
              <li><strong>Subjugate & Subjugate II:</strong> Basic attacks inflict Bloodflame on hit (1 turn on Subjugate, 2 turns on Subjugate II).</li>
              <li><strong>Decimate I–III Execution:</strong> Strikes all enemies, inflicting both Stun and Bloodflame. Features <strong>100% stun chance on lower-HP enemies</strong> (<span class="codeBadge">stunChanceOnLowerHp = 1.0</span>).</li>
              <li><strong>Colossal Sword of Scarlet King:</strong> Endgame greatsword with +124 CON, +7 DEX, and +50% Bloodflame damage bonus.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Rebalance 7: Whisper -->
        <div id="rebalance-whisper" class="rebalanceCard">
          <div class="rebalanceHeader">
            <img src={`${base}/images/unit_whisper.png`} alt="Whisper" class="sprite" width="36" height="36" />
            <div>
              <h3>7. Whisper Branch (Phantom Duelist & Precision Executioner)</h3>
              <span class="rebalanceArchetype">Innate +15% Dodge · DEF Ignore · Missing-HP Damage Amp · 3.0x Crit Eclipse</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="rebalanceBody">
            <p><strong>The Vanilla Problem:</strong> Squishy melee assassin with zero combat passives, relying on an impractical &lt;25% execution window that failed in long boss battles.</p>
            <p><strong>The Overhaul:</strong></p>
            <ul class="docsList">
              <li><strong>Branch Scope:</strong> Starts at Tier 5 (Spire Initiate) through Tier 9 (Whisper), leaving Tier 4 Assassin untouched.</li>
              <li><strong>Innate Evasion:</strong> Gains innate <strong>+15% dodge chance</strong> (<span class="codeBadge">flatDodgeChance = 0.15</span>) while preserving trap disarm (<span class="codeBadge">saboteur = true</span>). Daggers maintain 100% CON + 100% DEX scaling.</li>
              <li><strong>Phantom Instinct & Phantom Lethality Passives:</strong>
                <ul>
                  <li>Systematically targets the enemy with the lowest <strong>Relative % HP</strong> (<span class="codeBadge">TARGET_LOWEST_RELATIVE_ENEMY</span>).</li>
                  <li>Ignores <strong>20% to 40% of enemy DEF</strong> (20% T5 &rarr; 25% T6 &rarr; 30% T7 &rarr; 35% T8 &rarr; 40% T9).</li>
                  <li>Attacks deal up to <strong>+45% to +70% bonus damage</strong> based on the target's missing HP percentage.</li>
                </ul>
              </li>
              <li><strong>Eclipse Active Skill:</strong> Scales strictly <strong>+10% per tier</strong> (1.10x &rarr; 1.40x) with a massive <strong>3.0x Critical Strike Amplification</strong> and execution threshold with recast on kill (10% HP at T5 up to 25% HP at T9).</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Rebalance 8: Spirit Engraver -->
        <div id="rebalance-spirit-engraver" class="rebalanceCard">
          <div class="rebalanceHeader">
            <img src={`${base}/images/unit_spirit_engraver.png`} alt="Spirit Engraver" class="sprite" width="36" height="36" />
            <div>
              <h3>8. Spirit Engraver Branch (Deadly Finesse Flurry & Bleed Specialist)</h3>
              <span class="rebalanceArchetype">+100% Attack Speed (Guaranteed 2 Strikes) · 120 Bleed/Turn · Thousand Cuts II</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="rebalanceBody">
            <p><strong>The Overhaul:</strong></p>
            <ul class="docsList">
              <li><strong>Deadly Finesse Multi-Strike Rework:</strong> Overhauled the passive line (Meat Carver, Wounds Weaver, Hellish Sculptor, Spirit Engraver) into a dedicated flurry-of-cuts archetype:
                <ul>
                  <li><strong>Deadly Finesse I (Meat Carver):</strong> +50% Attack Speed (50% chance for a 2nd strike), -25% Basic Attack Amp.</li>
                  <li><strong>Deadly Finesse II (Wounds Weaver):</strong> +75% Attack Speed (75% chance for a 2nd strike), -35% Basic Attack Amp.</li>
                  <li><strong>Deadly Finesse III (Hellish Sculptor & Spirit Engraver):</strong> <strong>+100% Attack Speed (guaranteed 2 strikes every turn)</strong>, -50% Basic Attack Amp.</li>
                </ul>
              </li>
              <li><strong>Rapid Bleed Shredding:</strong> Spirit Engraver reliably applies <strong>120 Bleed per turn</strong> with basic attacks, rapidly melting enemy armor.</li>
              <li><strong>Unpenalized Active Skill:</strong> <em>Thousand Cuts II</em> active skill damage remains at 100% full power via Skill Amp. Retains full trap-disarming utility.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Rebalance 9: Celestial Rain -->
        <div id="rebalance-celestial-rain" class="rebalanceCard">
          <div class="rebalanceHeader">
            <img src={`${base}/images/unit_celestial_rain.png`} alt="Celestial Rain" class="sprite" width="36" height="36" />
            <div>
              <h3>9. Celestial Rain Branch (Sniper Archer Accuracy Rebalance)</h3>
              <span class="rebalanceArchetype">+30% Hit Chance Bonus · Removed Guaranteed Hits · Fair Evasion Dynamics</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="rebalanceBody">
            <p><strong>The Vanilla Problem:</strong> Marksman through Celestial Rain had unconditional 100% guaranteed hits (<span class="codeBadge">alwaysHits = true</span>) via Keen Vision, completely invalidating enemy evasion, dodge traits, and darkness mechanics across the entire game.</p>
            <p><strong>The Overhaul:</strong></p>
            <ul class="docsList">
              <li><strong>Branch Scope (T3–T9):</strong> Marksman (T3), Sureshot (T4), Fury (T5), Hailstorm (T6), Tempest (T7), Hurricane (T8), and Celestial Rain (T9).</li>
              <li><strong>Removed Guaranteed Hit:</strong> Removed innate <span class="codeBadge">alwaysHits = true</span> across all 7 units, allowing agile and evasive enemies to dodge arrows fairly.</li>
              <li><strong>+30% Flat Hit Chance:</strong> Granted a flat <span class="codeBadge">hitChanceBonus = 0.30</span> (+30% Hit Chance) across the branch, preserving supreme sniper accuracy without breaking combat rules.</li>
              <li><strong>Archer Accuracy Hierarchy:</strong> Celestial Rain retains +30% hit chance as the premier sniper line, while other archer branches (Riders, Poison Bow / Corrosive Wraith, and Alchemists) are tuned to +15% hit chance.</li>
              <li><strong>Focused Trait Synergy:</strong> Stacks additively with the <em>Focused</em> trait (+25%) for up to <strong>+55% Hit Chance</strong>. Guaranteed hit can still be unlocked through specific late-game gear (e.g. <em>Seeking Glass</em>, <em>Amulet of the Swordsman</em>).</li>
              <li><strong>Updated Keen Vision Tooltip:</strong> Skill description updated across all languages to <em>"Hit chance is increased by 30%"</em>.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- SECTION 3: SUMMONS & MINIONS -->
